(2514654, 342682, 3569, '<td valign="top">Yes.  Maceo glad you finally get a ribbon for all your lightning chases.  Great shot,placing, and well deserved ribbon.   Van</td>', 'Yes.  Maceo glad you finally get a ribbon for all your lightning chases.  Great shot,placing, and well deserved ribbon.   Van', '2006-06-14 01:23:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(2514665, 341669, 31133, '<td valign="top">Karen, you''re on a roll! Congratulations to you on this top 5 shot - whoooohhoooo!! I didn''t see this at all during voting, but would''ve rated it high. This is definately the first ever swan baby I''ve seen taking a ride on mom (or dad?). Great subject!</td>', 'Karen, you''re on a roll! Congratulations to you on this top 5 shot - whoooohhoooo!! I didn''t see this at all during voting, but would''ve rated it high. This is definately the first ever swan baby I''ve seen taking a ride on mom (or dad?). Great subject!', '2006-06-14 01:24:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(2514695, 344508, 48094, '<td valign="top">Wow, my first ribbon. Thanks to everyone for all the great comments and votes. <br/> <br/>The pic was taken at the Georgia Aquarium in Atlanta. I shoot there as often as possible, always fighting the low lighting. Usually the whale sharks stay at the top of the tank, so I was happy when this one dove down. All the fish fell into place and I was lucky to capture such a dynamic compostion. <br/> <br/>Editting consisited of:<br/>Raw conversion<br/>Cropping<br/>Levels<br/>Shadow / Highlight<br/>Curves<br/>Brightness / Contrast<br/>USM<br/>Neat Image<br/>Channel Mixer<br/> <br/>A lot of people commented on the choice of B&amp;W over color. Originally I was going to use a color image, but the color actually seemd to detract from the strength of the tonal range and compostion, so I decided to go B&amp;W. <br/> <br/>Thanks again!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-14 01:44:35.</i></td>', 'Wow, my first ribbon. Thanks to everyone for all the great comments and votes.  The pic was taken at the Georgia Aquarium in Atlanta. I shoot there as often as possible, always fighting the low lighting. Usually the whale sharks stay at the top of the tank, so I was happy when this one dove down. All the fish fell into place and I was lucky to capture such a dynamic compostion.  Editting consisited of:Raw conversionCroppingLevelsShadow / HighlightCurvesBrightness / ContrastUSMNeat ImageChannel Mixer A lot of people commented on the choice of B&W over color. Originally I was going to use a color image, but the color actually seemd to detract from the strength of the tonal range and compostion, so I decided to go B&W.  Thanks again!', '2006-06-14 01:28:29.000000', '2006-06-14 02:44:35.000000', 0),
(2514735, 344508, 16230, '<td valign="top">Excellent capture! Congratulations on your blue ribbon!</td>', 'Excellent capture! Congratulations on your blue ribbon!', '2006-06-14 01:36:54.000000', NULL, 0),
