(2518902, 342482, 55985, '<td valign="top">I would like to thank everyone for their comments/suggestions on this.  I originally had this taken with my 50mm f/1.4, but I got a 70-300 from UPS the same day the challenge ended, so this one may have been a bit too rushed and I should''ve moved the coin over to the side probably rather than a dead center.  In my 50mm version of this, you can tell rather well that the black thing is a spade that was used for recovering the coin, but I realized too late it looked odd in this one.  I''m trying to learn, hopefully I''ll keep progressing!</td>', 'I would like to thank everyone for their comments/suggestions on this.  I originally had this taken with my 50mm f/1.4, but I got a 70-300 from UPS the same day the challenge ended, so this one may have been a bit too rushed and I should''ve moved the coin over to the side probably rather than a dead center.  In my 50mm version of this, you can tell rather well that the black thing is a spade that was used for recovering the coin, but I realized too late it looked odd in this one.  I''m trying to learn, hopefully I''ll keep progressing!', '2006-06-15 01:35:17.000000', NULL, 0),
